### System Status
```bash
# Check all containers
docker compose ps

# Check container health
docker compose logs --tail=50 frontend-nx

# Check disk space
df -h

# Check memory usage
free -h
```

### Frontend Specific
```bash
# Check if dev server is responding
curl http://localhost:5000

# Check TypeScript compilation
cd ${EDUHUB_ROOT:-$PWD}/frontend-nx && npx tsc --noEmit

# Check linting
cd ${EDUHUB_ROOT:-$PWD}/frontend-nx && yarn lint
```

### Database Specific
```bash
# Check database connection
docker compose exec db_hasura psql -U postgres -d postgres -c "SELECT 1;"

# Check Hasura health
curl http://localhost:8080/healthz

# Check Keycloak health
curl http://localhost:28080/health
```

## Emergency Recovery

### Complete Reset
If nothing else works, perform a complete reset:

```bash
# Stop everything
docker compose down -v

# Remove all containers and images
docker compose down --rmi all --volumes --remove-orphans

# Clean Docker system
docker system prune -a

# Rebuild from scratch
docker compose up --build
```

### Backup Important Data
Before doing a complete reset, backup any important data:

```bash
# Backup database
docker compose exec db_hasura pg_dump -U postgres postgres > backup.sql

# Backup uploaded files
docker compose exec frontend-nx tar -czf /tmp/uploads.tar.gz /app/public/uploads
```

## Getting Help

### Log Collection
When reporting issues, collect these logs:

```bash
# System information
docker --version
docker compose --version
node --version
yarn --version

# Container logs
docker compose logs frontend-nx > frontend.log
docker compose logs hasura > hasura.log
docker compose logs db_hasura > database.log

# System resources
df -h > disk-usage.txt
free -h > memory-usage.txt
```

### Common Error Messages and Solutions

| Error Message | Likely Cause | Solution |
|---------------|--------------|----------|
| `Port 5000 is already in use` | Another service using port | Kill process or change port |
| `Cannot find module` | Missing dependencies | Run `yarn install` |
| `TypeError: swiper.params is undefined` | Swiper initialization issue | Restart containers |
| `GraphQL error: relation does not exist` | Database schema issue | Apply migrations |
| `Permission denied` | File permission issue | Fix file ownership |
| `Out of memory` | Insufficient resources | Increase Docker memory |